* Lab PSU V1 - simulation models for ngspice (KiCad built-in simulator)
* Behavioural models of ICs; parameters are first-order, not characterised. Not yet run in ngspice - tune before trusting results.

* MOSFETs Q1/Q2: IRFS4127PBF as a native ngspice VDMOS. Parameters taken from Infineon's own SPICE3 model (irfs4127pbf.spi):
*   Vto=4.9139 Kp=16.1662 Lambda=0.0358354 Rd=4.0m Rs=0.1m Rg=1.497 Cgs=5.25n (CGSO*W), Cgd 56p..300p (Infineon's 2.35n low-Vds peak made the solver stiff with probes), body diode Is=4.4e-7 N=1.41 Rb=1.83m Tt=100n Cjo=8.5n Bv=200
* Infineon's file stays in models/ as the reference; the original subcircuit is not used because its internal current-sensor / controlled-source
* loop cannot take the first transient step once KiCad wraps probe sources around it.
.model IRFS4127_VDM VDMOS(Vto=4.9139 Kp=16.1662 Lambda=0.0358354 Rd=4m Rs=0.1m Rg=1.497 Cgs=5.25n Cgdmax=300p Cgdmin=56p A=0.3 Cjo=8.5n Vj=0.5 M=0.774 Is=4.4e-7 N=1.41 Rb=1.83m tt=100n Bv=200 Ibv=2.5e-4)
.subckt IRFS4127_PRB 1 2 3
M1 1 2 3 3 IRFS4127_VDM
.ends IRFS4127_PRB

* ---- diodes
.model BAT54 D(Is=3e-8 N=1.1 Rs=0.6 Cjo=10p Vj=0.3 M=0.4 Bv=30 Ibv=1e-5)
.model ES1D D(Is=3e-9 N=1.9 Rs=0.15 Cjo=15p Bv=200 Ibv=1e-5 tt=25n)
.model BAS21 D(Is=2e-9 N=1.8 Rs=0.9 Cjo=2p Bv=250 Ibv=1e-6 tt=50n)
.model SS34 D(Is=5e-6 N=1.1 Rs=0.03 Cjo=300p Bv=40 Ibv=1e-4)
.model SS14 D(Is=3e-6 N=1.1 Rs=0.05 Cjo=150p Bv=40 Ibv=1e-4)

* ---- bidirectional TVS clamp: two anti-series junction diodes (built-in junction limiting, so Newton stays well-behaved); breakdown at 1 mA ~ 1.12 x standoff
.model TVS130_D D(Is=1e-12 N=1 Rs=1.5 Bv=145 Ibv=1m)
.model TVS110_D D(Is=1e-12 N=1 Rs=1.5 Bv=123 Ibv=1m)
.model TVS18_D D(Is=1e-12 N=1 Rs=0.3 Bv=20 Ibv=1m)
.subckt TVS130 a b
D1 a n TVS130_D
D2 b n TVS130_D
Ra a n 1G
Rb b n 1G
.ends TVS130
.subckt TVS110 a b
D1 a n TVS110_D
D2 b n TVS110_D
Ra a n 1G
Rb b n 1G
.ends TVS110
.subckt TVS18 a b
D1 a n TVS18_D
D2 b n TVS18_D
Ra a n 1G
Rb b n 1G
.ends TVS18

* ---- 4-terminal Kelvin shunt: force p1/p4, sense sp/sn
.subckt SHUNT4 p1 sp sn p4 params: r=10m
R1 p1 p4 {r}
Rsp sp p1 1m
Rsn sn p4 1m
.ends SHUNT4

* ---- IR2184 half-bridge driver: single input, internal dead time, bootstrap high side
.subckt IR2184_BEH in sd com lo vcc vs ho vb
Rfi in nfi 1k
Cfi nfi com 100p
Bho nho vs V = V(vb,vs)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(vcc,com)-8)/0.1)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(sd,com)-1.8)/0.05)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(nfi,com)-2.2)/0.05)))
Rho nho ho 2.5
Blo nlo com V = V(vcc,com)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(vcc,com)-8)/0.1)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(sd,com)-1.8)/0.05)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((1.1-V(nfi,com))/0.05)))
Rlo nlo lo 2.5
Rqcc vcc com 8k
Rqbs vb vs 120k
Rsd sd com 1meg
Rin2 in com 1meg
.ends IR2184_BEH

* ---- INA240A1: gain 20, out = 20*(inp-inn) + (ref1+ref2)/2, rail clamped, ~400 kHz bandwidth
.subckt INA240_BEH inp inn ref1 ref2 vp gnd out
Bo o1 gnd V = min(max(20*(V(inp,gnd)-V(inn,gnd)) + (V(ref1,gnd)+V(ref2,gnd))/2, 0.02), V(vp,gnd)-0.1)
Ro o1 out 100
Co out gnd 4n
Rip inp gnd 1meg
Rin inn gnd 1meg
Rq vp gnd 5k
.ends INA240_BEH

* ---- MCP6002 dual rail-to-rail op-amp: A0=2e3, slew ~0.4 V/us (GBW is higher than the real 1 MHz part, deliberately, to keep slew realistic)
.subckt OPA2_BEH out1 inm1 inp1 vee inp2 inm2 out2 vcc
Bo1 a1 vee V = V(vcc,vee)*(0.5+0.5*tanh(4e3*(V(inp1,vee)-V(inm1,vee))/V(vcc,vee)))
Rp1 a1 b1 1k
Cp1 b1 vee 8n
Ro1 b1 out1 100
Bo2 a2 vee V = V(vcc,vee)*(0.5+0.5*tanh(4e3*(V(inp2,vee)-V(inm2,vee))/V(vcc,vee)))
Rp2 a2 b2 1k
Cp2 b2 vee 8n
Ro2 b2 out2 100
Rq vcc vee 20k
Ri1 inp1 vee 1e11
Ri2 inp2 vee 1e11
Ri3 inm1 vee 1e11
Ri4 inm2 vee 1e11
.ends OPA2_BEH

* ---- LM393 dual open-drain comparator: output sinks (60 ohm) when inp < inm; smooth, no switch hysteresis
.subckt COMP2_OD out1 inm1 inp1 gnd inp2 inm2 out2 vcc
B1 out1 gnd I = V(out1,gnd)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(inm1,gnd)-V(inp1,gnd))/0.002)))/60
B2 out2 gnd I = V(out2,gnd)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(inm2,gnd)-V(inp2,gnd))/0.002)))/60
Rq vcc gnd 4k
Ri1 inp1 gnd 1e11
Ri2 inm1 gnd 1e11
Ri3 inp2 gnd 1e11
Ri4 inm2 gnd 1e11
.ends COMP2_OD

* ---- AP63203 (Diodes, 3.3 V fixed, 1.1 MHz, 2 A sync buck): switch-level, fixed-frequency peak-current-mode.
* ---- Datasheet values: Rds(on) HS 125 mR / LS 68 mR, Ipeak 2.8 A, UVLO 3.5 V rising / 440 mV hyst, EN 1.18 V / 1.10 V, soft-start 4 ms, VFB 3.30 V (internal 0.8 V ref + divider).
* ---- NOT modelled: spread spectrum, hiccup, thermal shutdown. Pins as the symbol: fb en in gnd sw bst
.model AP_BODY D(Is=1e-9 N=1.2 Rs=0.03 Cjo=100p tt=5n)
.model AP_BST D(Is=1e-9 N=1.2 Rs=3 Cjo=1p)
.subckt AP63203_SW fb en in gnd sw bst params: fsw=1.1meg
* enable / UVLO (input rising 3.5 V, falling ~3.06 V approximated by a single mid threshold)
Bok ok gnd V = (0.5*(1+tanh((V(in,gnd)-3.3)/0.05)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(en,gnd)-1.14)/0.02)))
Bvcc vcc gnd V = 4.7*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(in,gnd)-4.2)/0.1)))
* soft-start: 250 nA into 1 nF = 1 V in 4 ms, discharged when disabled
Css ss gnd 1n
Bss gnd ss I = V(ok)*250n*(0.5*(1-tanh((V(ss,gnd)-1)/0.005))) - (1-V(ok))*V(ss,gnd)/200
* error amp (gm 200 uS) compares FB/4.125 (=0.8 V at 3.3 V) with the ramped 0.8 V reference
Bea gnd comp I = 200u*(0.8*(0.5*(V(ss,gnd)+1-abs(V(ss,gnd)-1))) - V(fb,gnd)*0.8/3.3) - 1m*(V(comp,gnd)-1.45)*0.5*(1+tanh((V(comp,gnd)-1.45)/0.02)) - 1m*V(comp,gnd)*0.5*(1-tanh(V(comp,gnd)/0.02))
Rc comp cc 70k
Rcp comp gnd 100meg
Cc cc gnd 380p
Cp comp gnd 5p
Rfb fb gnd 1meg
Ren en gnd 10meg
* clock: short pulse at the crest of a sine (about 70 ns), and an analog slope-compensation ramp sl (0..1) that is pulled to 0 during that pulse (continuous, no sawtooth jump)
Bclk clk gnd V = 0.5*(1+tanh((sin(6.28318530718*{fsw}*time)-0.97)/0.01))
Csl sl gnd 1p
Rsl sl gnd 1g
Bsl gnd sl I = 1p*({fsw}*(1-V(clk,gnd)) - 5e7*V(clk,gnd)*V(sl,gnd))
* set/reset latch on node q: reset dominant and regenerative (a cubic term pushes q to 0 or 1, like a real flip-flop); no new cycle while comp is at its floor (power-save skipping) or while the low-side valley current exceeds 3.2 A
Cq q gnd 1p
Rq q gnd 1g
Bq gnd q I = 1p*1e8*(V(ok)*V(clk,gnd)*(1-V(rst,gnd))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(comp,gnd)-0.05)/0.02)))*(1-0.5*(1+tanh((-V(sw,gnd)*14.7*V(ls,gnd)-3.2)/0.05)))*(1-V(q,gnd)) - V(rst,gnd)*V(q,gnd) + 3*V(q,gnd)*(1-V(q,gnd))*(2*V(q,gnd)-1))
Bsum sum gnd V = 0.4*V(ihs,gnd) + 0.18*V(sl,gnd)
* reset: peak current reached, 2.8 A limit or max duty, after the 80 ns minimum on-time (soft OR)
Bcmp cmp gnd V = 1-(1-0.5*(1+tanh((V(sum,gnd)-V(comp,gnd))/0.01)))*(1-0.5*(1+tanh((V(ihs,gnd)-2.8)/0.02)))*(1-0.5*(1+tanh((V(sl,gnd)-0.92)/0.01)))
Brst rst gnd V = (0.5*(1+tanh((V(sl,gnd)-0.08)/0.01)))*V(cmp,gnd)
Bqc qc gnd V = 0.5*(1+tanh((V(q,gnd)-0.5)/0.05))
* dead time: delayed copy; HS needs both high, LS needs both low (products stay smooth)
Rd qc qd 4
Cd qd gnd 2p
Bhs hs gnd V = V(qc,gnd)*V(qd,gnd)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(bst,sw)-2.5)/0.1)))
Bls ls gnd V = (1-V(qc,gnd))*(1-V(qd,gnd))*V(ok)
* power switches as gated conductances
Bhsp in sw I = V(in,sw)*(8*V(hs,gnd)+1e-9)
Blsp sw gnd I = V(sw,gnd)*(14.7*V(ls,gnd)+1e-9)
Bihs ihs gnd V = 0.5*(V(in,sw)*8*V(hs,gnd)+sqrt(V(in,sw)*8*V(hs,gnd)*V(in,sw)*8*V(hs,gnd)+1e-4))
Dbody gnd sw AP_BODY
Dbst vcc bst AP_BST
Csw sw gnd 100p
Rbst bst gnd 10meg
Rin in gnd 5meg
.ends AP63203_SW

* ---- AP63203 (Diodes, 3.3 V fixed, 2 A sync buck), cycle-averaged: no 1.1 MHz switching, so the transient runs at normal step sizes.
* ---- Real-part numbers: UVLO 3.5 V rising, EN 1.14 V, 4 ms soft-start, VFB 3.30 V, peak limit 2.8 A, ~0.1 ohm conduction loss, ~0.12 W switching/driver loss (~90 % at 1 A, 12 V to 3.3 V), Iq 22 uA.
* ---- The switch node sw is driven as an average voltage by a fast inner current loop (peak-current-mode equivalent: demand = comp/0.4 A/V - half ripple).
* ---- Not modelled: ripple, spread spectrum, hiccup, thermal shutdown, power-save skipping (it behaves as forced-PWM, current may reverse). Pins as the symbol: fb en in gnd sw bst
.subckt AP63203_AVG fb en in gnd sw bst params: lnom=4.7u
Bok ok gnd V = (0.5*(1+tanh((V(in,gnd)-3.3)/0.05)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(en,gnd)-1.14)/0.02)))
Css ss gnd 1n
Bss gnd ss I = V(ok)*250n*(0.5*(1-tanh((V(ss,gnd)-1)/0.005))) - (1-V(ok))*V(ss,gnd)/200
Bea gnd comp I = 200u*(0.8*(0.5*(V(ss,gnd)+1-abs(V(ss,gnd)-1))) - V(fb,gnd)*0.8/3.3) - 1m*(V(comp,gnd)-1.45)*0.5*(1+tanh((V(comp,gnd)-1.45)/0.02)) - 1m*V(comp,gnd)*0.5*(1-tanh(V(comp,gnd)/0.02))
Rc comp cc 70k
Rcp comp gnd 100meg
Cc cc gnd 380p
Cp comp gnd 5p
Rfb fb gnd 1meg
Ren en gnd 10meg
* average inductor-current demand, limited to the 2.8 A peak limit less half the ripple
Bid id gnd V = V(ok)*0.5*(V(max0,gnd)+2.57-abs(V(max0,gnd)-2.57))
Bmx max0 gnd V = 0.5*((V(comp,gnd)/0.4-0.23)+abs(V(comp,gnd)/0.4-0.23))
* inner current loop: switch-node voltage = output voltage (feed-forward) + k*(demand - iL), k = 2*pi*150 kHz*L, kept inside 0..0.9*Vin
Bsw nint gnd V = V(ok)*0.5*(V(vhi,gnd)+0.9*V(in,gnd)-abs(V(vhi,gnd)-0.9*V(in,gnd)))
Bhi vhi gnd V = 0.5*(V(vlo,gnd)+abs(V(vlo,gnd)))
Blo vlo gnd V = V(fb,gnd) + 6.283185*150k*{lnom}*(V(id,gnd)-I(Vz))
Vz nint n2 0
Rs n2 sw 0.1
* input current: power taken from the bus / Vin, plus switching loss and Iq
Bin in gnd I = V(ok)*(0.5*(V(P,gnd)+abs(V(P,gnd))))/max(V(in,gnd),3) + 22u + V(ok)*0.12/max(V(in,gnd),3)
BP P gnd V = V(nint)*I(Vz)
Rbst bst gnd 10meg
Rin in gnd 5meg
.ends AP63203_AVG

* ---- STM32G474 control firmware stand-in (NOT the MCU): feed-forward duty = Vset/Vbus + slow PI trim,
* ---- CV/CC by taking the smaller of the voltage and current errors, fixed-frequency triangle-carrier PWM (algebraic carrier: no PULSE breakpoints), DAC thresholds.
* ---- Only the pins the power stage uses are modelled; params: vset [V], iset [A], ovp [V], ocp [A], ki [1/s]
.subckt MCU_BEH vdd vss vout iout vin drv_in drv_in2 drv_en fault_n ovp_dac ocp_dac relay_en params: vset=50 iset=3 ovp=110 ocp=6 ki=3 kd=1u tss=3m fsw=100k tstab=20m
Bon on vss V = (0.5*(1+tanh((V(vdd,vss)-2.5)/0.05)))
Bvsp vsp vss V = {vset}*min(max(time-400u,0)/{tss},1)
Bvm vm vss V = V(vout,vss)*34.22
Bvb vbus vss V = max(V(vin,vss)*51,20)
Bim im vss V = (V(iout,vss)-V(vdd,vss)/2)/0.2
Bev ev vss V = V(vsp)-V(vmf)
Bei ei vss V = ({iset}-V(im))*5
Bem em vss V = 0.5*(V(ev)+V(ei)-sqrt((V(ev)-V(ei))*(V(ev)-V(ei))+0.01))
Brdy rdy vss V = (0.5*(1+tanh((time-400u-{tss})/50u)))
Bint vss ctl I = {ki}*V(em)*V(run)*V(rdy)*(1-(0.5*(1+tanh((V(ctl)-0.3)/0.01)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(em))/0.01)))-(0.5*(1+tanh((-0.3-V(ctl))/0.01)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((-V(em))/0.01))))
Cint ctl vss 1 ic=0
Rctl ctl vss 1e9
Rf vm vmf 1
Cf vmf vss 1p
* RC differentiator (10 us lag) instead of ddt(), which amplifies noise as the solver shrinks the timestep
Rdv vmf vf2 1k
Cdv vf2 vss 10n
Bdv dvm vss V = (V(vmf)-V(vf2,vss))/10u
Brun run vss V = V(on)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(vbus)-30)/1)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((time-400u)/5u)))
Bm m vss V = V(run)*min(max(V(vsp)/V(vbus) + V(ctl) - {kd}*V(dvm), 0), 4.5)
Bd d vss V = min(0.9*V(m), 0.9)
Bd2 d2 vss V = 0.9/max(V(m), 1)
Bsaw saw vss V = 0.5+asin(sin(6.28318530718*{fsw}*time))/3.14159265359
Bpwm drv_in vss V = 3.3*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(d)-V(saw)-0.005)/0.002)))
Bpwm2 drv_in2 vss V = 3.3*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(d2)-V(saw)-0.005)/0.002)))
Ben drv_en vss V = V(run)*3.3
Bov ovp_dac vss V = {ovp}/34.22
Boc ocp_dac vss V = V(vdd,vss)/2 + {ocp}*0.2
* ---- Output relay enable (firmware): closes only after the measured output (ADC on VOUT) has stayed within 5 % + 0.5 V of the setpoint, or sat at the current limit (CC),
* ---- for tstab with FAULT_N high and the soft-start finished; opens again if that is lost for a few ms.
Bgd gd vss V = max(0.5*(1+tanh((0.05*{vset}+0.5-abs(V(vm)-V(vsp)))/0.05)), 0.5*(1+tanh((V(im)-0.95*{iset})/0.05)))*V(rdy)*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(fault_n,vss)-1.65)/0.1)))
Ctm tmr vss 1 ic=0
Btm vss tmr I = V(run)*V(gd)*(0.5*(1-tanh((V(tmr)-1)/0.01)))/{tstab} - (1-V(run)*V(gd))*tanh(max(V(tmr),0)/0.01)/2m
Rtm tmr vss 1e9
Brl relay_en vss V = 3.3*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(tmr)-0.98)/0.005)))
Rrl relay_en vss 1G
Rfl fault_n vss 1G
Rvo vout vss 1G
.ends MCU_BEH

* ======================= MAINS SIDE MODELS (MainsInput sheet) =======================
* Toroid 230V : 2 x 45V 500VA (Vigortronix VTX-146-500-145 datasheet: 6 % regulation, 5.56 A series, 68 K rise).
* Linear model (no core saturation, so switch-on inrush is only roughly right). Pins: 1=AA 2=AB (primary), 3=SA 4=SB 5=SC 6=SD.
* Interwinding capacitance 2 x 300 pF (also keeps the isolated secondary common-mode well conditioned).
* Per-winding no-load 47.7 V (45 V x 1.06): turns ratio 0.2074; Rp=2R, Rs=0.4R each (+ ~0.1R reflected) reproduces the 6 % regulation.
.subckt TRAFO_500 aa ab sa sb sc sd params: lp=10 rp=1.2 rs=0.12 k=0.9995 n=0.2074
Rp aa ap {rp}
Lp ap ab {lp}
Rs1 sa s1 {rs}
Ls1 s1 sb {lp*n*n}
Rs2 sc s2 {rs}
Ls2 s2 sd {lp*n*n}
K1 Lp Ls1 Ls2 {k}
Cps1 ap s1 300p
Cps2 ap s2 300p
.ends TRAFO_500

* Bridge rectifier KBPC-class, 25 A 1000 V (Vf ~0.97 V at 5 A). Pins: 1=+ 2=- 3=AC 4=AC.
.model DBR D(Is=5e-8 N=1.9 Rs=0.012 Cjo=10p Bv=1000 Ibv=5e-6 tt=0)
.subckt BRIDGE_KBPC dcp dcn ac1 ac2
D1 ac1 dcp DBR
D2 ac2 dcp DBR
D3 dcn ac1 DBR
D4 dcn ac2 DBR
.ends BRIDGE_KBPC

* Electrolytic with ESR. Pins 1=+ 2=-
.subckt CAP_ESR p n params: c=3300u esr=0.03
C1 p m {c}
R1 m n {esr}
.ends CAP_ESR

* MOV S14K275 (430 V @ 1 mA, ~I ~ V^25). Pins 1,2
.subckt MOV275 a b
Bt a b I = 1m*(exp(min((V(a,b)-430)/17,40)) - exp(min((-V(a,b)-430)/17,40)))
Rl a b 1G
.ends MOV275

* Mains switch DPST, closed (1 mOhm per pole). Pins: 1-2 and 3-4
.subckt SW_DPST_ON p1 p2 p3 p4
Ra p3 p4 1m
Rb p1 p2 1m
.ends SW_DPST_ON

* Common-mode choke 2 x 3.3 mH, k=0.99, 40 mOhm per winding. Pins 1-2 and 3-4
.subckt CMCHOKE a1 a2 b1 b2
Ra a1 am 40m
La am a2 3.3m
Rb b1 bm 40m
Lb bm b2 3.3m
K1 La Lb 0.99
.ends CMCHOKE

* NTC inrush limiter with self-heating: R falls from r25 (cold) to rhot as dissipated energy (node e, joules) builds up; cools with tau ~100 s. e_amb = stored heat at start in J (0 = cold start, ~100 = fully warm).
.subckt NTC_INRUSH a b params: r25=5 rhot=0.3 e0=25 e_amb=0
Br rr 0 V = {rhot}+({r25}-{rhot})*exp(-V(e)/{e0})
Bi a b I = V(a,b)/V(rr)
Bp 0 e I = V(a,b)*V(a,b)/V(rr)
Ce e 0 1
Rl e 0 100
Bamb 0 e I = {e_amb}/100
.ends NTC_INRUSH

* Mean Well IRM-10-12 (behavioural): 12 V (0.1 ohm) once the rectified-mean mains input exceeds ~70 V, fixed ~8 W input draw. Pins 1=AC/N 2=AC/L 3=-Vo 4=+Vo
.subckt IRM_10_12 acn acl vn vp
Rin acl acn 6.6k
Benv env 0 V = abs(V(acl,acn))
Renv env e2 1k
Cenv e2 0 100u
Bv vpi vn V = 12*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(e2)-70)/10)))
Rout vpi vp 0.1
.ends IRM_10_12

* IRM-10-12 stand-in fed from the rectified toroid bus (+HV) instead of mains: the AC pins are unused, so 12 V and the 3.3 V buck behind it follow the transformer.
* 12 V (0.1 ohm) once +HV exceeds ~12 V; input draw = Pout/0.8 + 0.3 W from +HV. Pins 1=AC/N 2=AC/L 3=-Vo 4=+Vo
.global +HV
.subckt IRM_10_12_HV acn acl vn vp
Benv env 0 V = V(+HV)
Renv env e2 100
Cenv e2 0 10u
Bv vpi vn V = 12*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(e2)-12)/2)))
Rout vpi vp 0.1
Bin +HV vn I = (0.5*(1+tanh((V(e2)-12)/2)))*(V(vpi,vn)*(V(vpi,vp)/0.1)/0.8 + 0.3)/max(V(+HV,vn),10)
.ends IRM_10_12_HV

* Constant-power load standing in for the buck stage (draws pwr/V from the bus once t > tstart). Pins 1=+ 2=-
.subckt CPL_LOAD p n params: pload=540 tstart=60m tramp=2m vmin=50
B1 p n I = {pload}*min(max((time-{tstart})/{tramp},0),1)/max(V(p,n),{vmin})
.ends CPL_LOAD

* ---- 2N7002 (relay coil driver): SOT-23 N-MOSFET, Vth ~2.1 V, Rds(on) ~2 ohm at 4.5 V (datasheet-class values, native VDMOS)
* level-1 NMOS + body diode (same Vto/Kp/Rd/Rs/caps/diode data): the native VDMOS version made ngspice abort with 'timestep too small' in the AnalogCtl ramp oscillator
.model N2N7002_L1 NMOS(Level=1 Vto=2.1 Kp=0.25 Lambda=0.01 Rd=0.7 Rs=0.1 Cgso=22p Cgdo=4p)
.model N2N7002_DB D(Is=1e-9 N=1.3 Rs=1 Cjo=10p Vj=0.7 M=0.4 Bv=60 Ibv=1e-6)
.subckt N2N7002 d g s
M1 d g s s N2N7002_L1 W=1 L=1
Dbody s d N2N7002_DB
.ends N2N7002

* ---- LMR33630A (Buck3V3 sheet): IDEAL 3.3 V source for simulation. Present from t=0 (no UVLO, enable or soft-start), 50 mohm output impedance.
* ---- The 400 kHz vendor model LMR33630A_TRANS_ng.lib is ~100x slower; select it on U201 in Buck3V3.kicad_sch when the buck itself is being checked.
* ---- Pins as LMR33630A_DDA / the KiCad symbol: 1=gnd 2=vin 3=en 4=pg 5=fb 6=vcc 7=boot 8=sw.  vout is fixed (does not follow the FB divider).
.subckt LMR33630A_BEH gnd vin en pg fb vcc boot sw params: vout=3.3
Bsw nsw gnd V = {vout}
Rsw nsw sw 0.05
Bvcc nvcc gnd V = 5
Rvcc nvcc vcc 100
Rvin vin gnd 1meg
Rfb fb gnd 1meg
Rbt boot gnd 1meg
Rpg pg gnd 1meg
Ren en gnd 1meg
.ends LMR33630A_BEH

* ---- SPST-NO power relay, 12 V coil (400 ohm, 0.2 H): pulls in above 9 V after ~8 ms, drops out below 1.2 V after ~4 ms, contact 10 mohm. No bounce, no contact rating.
.subckt RELAY_SPST_12V c1 c2 k1 k2 params: rcoil=400 lcoil=0.2 vpu=9 vdo=1.2 ton=8m toff=4m ron=10m
Rc c1 cx {rcoil}
Lc cx c2 {lcoil}
Cq q 0 1u
Rq q 0 1e9
Bq 0 q I = 1u*((0.5*(1+tanh((V(c1,c2)-{vpu})/0.2)))*(1-V(q))/{ton} - (0.5*(1+tanh(({vdo}-V(c1,c2))/0.2)))*V(q)/{toff})
Bk k1 k2 I = V(k1,k2)*((0.5*(1+tanh((V(q)-0.5)/0.05)))/{ron} + 1e-9)
.ends RELAY_SPST_12V

* ======================= ANALOG CONTROLLER MODELS (AnalogCtl sheet) =======================
* Op-amp macromodel: single dominant pole (GBW), slew limit, output swing, input bias, offset. Single-supply, output stage = B-source + Rout.
* ngspice: gm [S] sets the gain stage; Ca gives the GBW, the tanh output current limit gives the slew rate
.subckt OPAMP_CORE out inm inp vee vcc params: gbw=1meg sr=0.3meg vos=2m ib=45n voh=1.5 vol=0.02 rout=50 a0=1e5 iq=350u gm=1m
.param cap={gm/(6.283185*gbw)} imx={sr*gm/(6.283185*gbw)} rra={a0/gm}
Bib1 inp vee I = {ib}
Bib2 inm vee I = {ib}
Bg vee a I = {imx}*tanh({gm}*(V(inp,vee)-V(inm,vee)+{vos})/{imx})
Ra a vee {rra}
Ca a vee {cap}
Bcl vee a I = -1m*(V(a,vee)-(V(vcc,vee)-{voh}))*0.5*(1+tanh((V(a,vee)-(V(vcc,vee)-{voh}))/20m)) - 1m*(V(a,vee)-{vol})*0.5*(1-tanh((V(a,vee)-{vol})/20m))
Bo o vee V = V(a,vee)
Ro o out {rout}
Iqq vcc vee {iq}
.ends OPAMP_CORE

* LM358 (dual): GBW 1 MHz, SR 0.3 V/us, Vos 2 mV, Ib 45 nA, output to Vcc-1.5 V, sinks to ~20 mV.  Pins as the symbol/OPA2_BEH: 1=out1 2=inm1 3=inp1 4=vee 5=inp2 6=inm2 7=out2 8=vcc
.subckt LM358 out1 inm1 inp1 vee inp2 inm2 out2 vcc
XA out1 inm1 inp1 vee vcc OPAMP_CORE gbw=1meg sr=0.3meg vos=2m ib=45n voh=1.5 vol=0.02 rout=50 iq=350u
XB out2 inm2 inp2 vee vcc OPAMP_CORE gbw=1meg sr=0.3meg vos=2m ib=45n voh=1.5 vol=0.02 rout=50 iq=350u
.ends LM358

* Open-collector comparator core: output transistor sinks (ron) when inp < inm, response time tpd, offset vos, input bias ib
.subckt COMP_OC out inm inp vee vcc params:  tpd=1.3u vos=2m ib=25n ron=60
.param ctd={tpd/2200}
Bib1 inp vee I = {ib}
Bib2 inm vee I = {ib}
Ri1 inp vee 1e11
Ri2 inm vee 1e11
Bd x vee V = 0.5*(1+tanh((V(inp,vee)-V(inm,vee)-{vos})/5m))
Rd x xd 1k
Cd xd vee {ctd}
Bo out vee I = V(out,vee)*((1-V(xd,vee))/{ron}+1n)
Iqq vcc vee 0.2m
.ends COMP_OC

* LM393 (dual): tpd 1.3 us, 16 mA sink.  Pins: 1=out1 2=inm1 3=inp1 4=vee 5=inp2 6=inm2 7=out2 8=vcc
.subckt LM393 out1 inm1 inp1 vee inp2 inm2 out2 vcc
XA out1 inm1 inp1 vee vcc COMP_OC tpd=1.3u vos=2m ib=25n ron=60
XB out2 inm2 inp2 vee vcc COMP_OC tpd=1.3u vos=2m ib=25n ron=60
.ends LM393

* LM311 (single, faster): tpd 200 ns.  Pins as the KiCad symbol: 1=GND(emitter) 2=IN+ 3=IN- 4=V- 5=BAL 6=STRB 7=OUT 8=V+
.subckt LM311 gnd inp inm vee bal strb out vcc
X1 out inm inp gnd vcc COMP_OC tpd=0.2u vos=2m ib=100n ron=20
Rb bal gnd 1g
Rs strb gnd 1g
Rv vee gnd 0.1
.ends LM311

* NE555 (bipolar, astable/ramp use): set when TRIG < CTRL/2, reset when THRES > CTRL, discharge transistor on while output low, internal 3 x 5k divider.
* Pins: 1=GND 2=TRIG 3=OUT 4=RESET 5=CTRL 6=THRES 7=DISCH 8=VCC
.subckt NE555 gnd trig out rst ctrl thr dis vcc
Rd1 vcc ctrl 5k
Rd2 ctrl lo 5k
Rd3 lo gnd 5k
Cq q gnd 1p
Rq q gnd 1g
Bs s gnd V = 0.5*(1+tanh((V(lo,gnd)-V(trig,gnd))/2m))
Br r gnd V = max(0.5*(1+tanh((V(thr,gnd)-V(ctrl,gnd))/2m)),0.5*(1-tanh((V(rst,gnd)-0.7)/0.05)))
Bq gnd q I = 1p*1e8*(V(s,gnd)*(1-V(r,gnd))*(1-V(q,gnd)) - V(r,gnd)*V(q,gnd) + 3*V(q,gnd)*(1-V(q,gnd))*(2*V(q,gnd)-1))
Bo outi gnd V = V(vcc,gnd)*V(q,gnd)
Ro outi out 20
Bdis dis gnd I = V(dis,gnd)*(0.5*(1-tanh((V(q,gnd)-0.5)/0.1)))/10
Iqq vcc gnd 3m
.ends NE555

* TL431: 2.495 V reference. Pins as the KiCad symbol: 1=REF 2=A 3=K.  Cathode current rises steeply once REF exceeds 2.495 V; 2 uA reference input current.
.subckt TL431 ref a k
Bi1 ref a I = 2u
Bk k a I = 0.5*(V(x,a)+sqrt(V(x,a)*V(x,a)+1e-6))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(k,a)-1)/0.1)))
Bx x a V = 1e3*(V(ref,a)-2.495)
.ends TL431

* Potentiometer (front-panel knob): a - w - b, total r, wiper position pos (0..1 from a). Optional step: moves to pos2 over 1 ms starting at tstep (leave pos2=pos for a static knob)
.subckt POT3 a w b params: r=10k pos=0.5 pos2=0.5 tstep=1
Bp p 0 V = max(min({pos}+({pos2}-{pos})*min(max((time-{tstep})/1m,0),1),0.999),0.001)
Rpd p 0 1g
B1 a w I = V(a,w)/({r}*V(p))
B2 w b I = V(w,b)/({r}*(1-V(p)))
.ends POT3

* Front-panel toggle switch, closes at time ton (emulates the user flipping it), ron when closed
.subckt SW_TIMED a b params: ton=1m ron=20m
Bsw a b I = V(a,b)*(0.5*(1+tanh((time-{ton})/20u))/{ron}+1n)
.ends SW_TIMED

.model LED_RED D(Is=1e-20 N=2 Rs=5 Cjo=30p Bv=5 Ibv=10u)

.model D1N4148 D(Is=2.5n N=1.75 Rs=0.6 Cjo=2p Vj=0.6 M=0.4 Bv=100 Ibv=100u tt=4n)
.model BZX84C5V1 D(Is=1e-14 N=1 Rs=15 Cjo=60p Bv=5.1 Ibv=5m)
.model BC857 PNP(Is=2e-14 Bf=250 Vaf=80 Ikf=0.1 Rb=10 Re=1 Rc=1 Cje=10p Cjc=6p Tf=0.5n Tr=30n)

* subckt wrapper so KiCad can map the BJT pins: c b e
.subckt BC857_S c b e
Q1 c b e BC857
.ends BC857_S
